# This repo is edited on Windows but only ever runs on Linux (servers, CI
# runners, the AppImage). Shell scripts and the `run:` blocks of workflows are
# executed verbatim, so a CRLF that sneaks into the repo becomes a literal
# carriage return in the command line — `$'\r': command not found`, or a
# trailing \r glued to the last exec argument. Normalise text to LF on commit
# and check it out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by EOL conversion.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.zip binary
*.db binary
